---
import BaseLayout from "~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Research"
  description="Computational design tooling at the heart of the studio's daily workflow."
>
  <section class="section section--hero container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Research</p>
    <h1>Tools as <em>instruments</em>, not as the design.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Computational tools earn their place when they let the studio test more
      alternatives, more honestly, in less time. The list below is short on
      purpose: only the instruments used regularly, with a note on what each is
      asked to do.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section container">
    <ol class="tools">
      <li>
        <header>
          <h3>Sketchup</h3>
          <p class="eyebrow">Form &amp; massing · daily</p>
        </header>
        <p>
          The studio's everyday surface for thinking in three dimensions —
          fast enough to keep up with conversation, accurate enough to feed
          schematic drawings.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <header>
          <h3>Grasshopper</h3>
          <p class="eyebrow">Computational geometry · weekly</p>
        </header>
        <p>
          Used where a problem has many alternatives: facade rhythms, terrace
          stepping, daylight studies. The aim is to widen the search, not to
          generate novelty for its own sake.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <header>
          <h3>Rhino</h3>
          <p class="eyebrow">Detail geometry · per project</p>
        </header>
        <p>
          The engine behind Grasshopper, plus the place where complex surfaces
          and detail geometry get resolved before drawings are issued.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="research-note">
      <p>
        <strong>What's not on this list.</strong> Tools that look impressive
        but are rarely used in real schemes don't earn a place. The studio
        prefers a small kit, used well.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h1 em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 300;
  }
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.4vw, 1.2rem);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }
  .tools {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    counter-reset: t;
  }
  .tools li {
    counter-increment: t;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: var(--space-3) 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 4rem 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .tools li::before {
    content: "0" counter(t);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--fg-subtle);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .tools header h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .tools header .eyebrow {
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }
  .tools li > p {
    grid-column: 2 / 3;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .research-note {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    padding: var(--space-3);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .research-note p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .research-note strong {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
</style>
